              "value": "You are a precise matcher for Expenditure Type. Return JSON only.\n\nInputs\n- candidateResources: {$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_CODE_PREPARE_EXPENDITURE_TYPE_MATCH_INPUTS.$output.result.candidateResources}\n- existingResources: {$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_CODE_PREPARE_EXPENDITURE_TYPE_MATCH_INPUTS.$output.result.existingResources}\n- sourceList: {$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_BO_FETCH_EXPENDITURE_TYPE_SOURCE_LIST.$output.items}\n\nRules\n1. candidateResources already contains only entries where ResourceType is exactly Expenditure Type.\n2. existingResources already contains only PRBS resources where FormatName is exactly Expenditure Type.\n3. If candidateResources is empty or sourceList is empty, return {\"matches\":[],\"newResources\":[]}.\n4. Normalize matching text by lowercasing, trimming, replacing underscores and hyphens with spaces, removing punctuation (.,;:/\\-_'\"()[]{}), and collapsing repeated spaces.\n5. Build candidate names from candidateResources[].ResourceName and dedupe them by normalized form.\n6. Choose matches only from sourceList. Prefer exact normalized matches, then strong token overlaps, then clear semantic abbreviations when obvious.\n7. Extract the chosen display name from the first non-empty source key among [\"ProjectRoleName\", \"ExpTypeName\", \"ExpenditureTypeName\", \"ExpenditureCategoryName\", \"CategoryName\", \"NonlaborResourceName\", \"Name\", \"RoleName\"]. Extract Id from the first non-empty source key among [\"ProjectRoleId\", \"ExpTypeId\", \"ExpenditureTypeId\", \"ExpenditureCategoryId\", \"ExpCategoryId\", \"NonlaborResourceId\", \"Id\"].\n8. Determine PresentInExisting using the chosen Id when existingResources carries a comparable Id key; otherwise compare normalized chosen display name against existingResources using the first non-empty existing value among [\"ExpenditureTypeName\", \"ResourceName\"].\n9. If a candidate has no good match in sourceList, omit that candidate from both matches and newResources.\n10. Build matches in this exact shape: {\"Type\":\"Expenditure Type\",\"Id\":\"string or empty\",\"Name\":\"chosen display name\",\"PresentInExisting\":true|false}.\n11. For each match with PresentInExisting=false, add one object to newResources using this exact payload shape: {\"ResourceClassName\":\"Financial resources\",\"FormatName\":\"Expenditure Type\",\"ExpenditureTypeName\":\"Name\"}\n12. Never add unmatched candidate names directly to newResources.\n13. Do not invent source entries. Do not add commentary. Return only the JSON object with keys matches and newResources."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"matches\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\"}},\"newResources\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\"}}}}",
