            {
              "id": "1775422001407_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a precise matcher for Project Role. Return JSON only.\n\nInputs\n- candidateResources: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_CODE_PREPARE_PROJECT_ROLE_MATCH_INPUTS.$output.result.candidateResources}}\n- existingResources: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_CODE_PREPARE_PROJECT_ROLE_MATCH_INPUTS.$output.result.existingResources}}\n- rolesFromLov: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_BO_FETCH_PROJECT_ROLE_SOURCE_LIST.$output.items}}\n\nRules\n1. candidateResources already contains only entries where ResourceType is exactly Project Role.\n2. existingResources already contains only PRBS resources where FormatName is exactly Project Role.\n3. If candidateResources is empty or rolesFromLov is empty, return {\"matches\":[],\"newResources\":[]}.\n4. Matching is semantic and token-based: case-insensitive; trim; remove punctuation (.,;:/\\-_'\"()[]{}); collapse repeated spaces; treat underscores and spaces equivalently.\n5. Treat pluralization and basic morphology as equivalent when clearly role-related. Recognize these common synonyms/abbreviations: PM ��� project manager, QA ��� quality assurance, DBA ��� database administrator, PI ��� principal investigator, Admin ��� administrator, BA ��� business analyst, PO ��� product owner, SME ��� subject matter expert.\n6. Prefer exact whole-token or clear head-term matches. Avoid weak substring noise.\n7. Compare against ProjectRoleName first; use RoleName only as a fallback for matching.\n8. Build one best match per candidate. Deduplicate by ProjectRoleId.\n9. PresentInExisting is true when existingResources contains the same ProjectRoleId or the same normalized ProjectRoleName.\n10. If a candidate has no good role match in rolesFromLov, omit that candidate from both matches and newResources.\n11. Build matches in this exact shape: {\"Type\":\"Project Role\",\"Id\":\"ProjectRoleId as string\",\"Name\":\"ProjectRoleName\",\"PresentInExisting\":true|false}.\n12. For each match with PresentInExisting=false, add one object to newResources using this exact payload shape: {\"ResourceClassName\":\"Labor\",\"FormatName\":\"Project Role\",\"ProjectRoleName\":\"Name\"}.\n13. Never add unmatched candidate names directly to newResources.\n14. Return only the JSON object with keys matches and newResources."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"matches\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\"}},\"newResources\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\"}}}}",
